<title>USA: White House sees low inflation, unemployment.</title>
<headline>White House sees low inflation, unemployment.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said Thursday it believes the fundamentals of the U.S. economy are strong and will produce continued low inflation and unemployment.</p>
<p>Asked if he was concerned by the December producer price index released earlier on Thursday showing a 0.5 percent increase to give a 2.8 percent rise for the whole of 1996, White House spokesman Mike McCurry told reporters: &quot;We think we have strong fundamentals in the economy that will produce continued economic growth with low rates of inflation and low rates of unemployment.&quot;</p>
</text>
